# Oversized binary assets — exceed GitHub's per-file limits and shouldn't
# ship with the repo. Use external storage / asset CDN for these.
public/assets/Exports/gambit-full-export-*.json
public/assets/Units/unit frames/Mythic Spellbook units/Last units/Bonus units/Newunits.zip

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 🗃 STAGING / SOURCE MATERIAL — mirrors public/.assetsignore
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# These are the files Cloudflare already refuses to upload (over its 25 MiB
# per-asset cap) plus raw editor sources. They live on disk, they are NOT
# served, and they must not enter git — there is ~3.4 GB of them, and a
# `git add -A` sweeping it in times out mid-run and leaves a stale
# .git/index.lock behind. That is not hypothetical; it happened.
#
# ⚠ This does NOT untrack anything already committed — gitignore only
# affects files git is not yet following.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.psd
# Raw 3D model sources. Runtime models are served from the Supabase `models`
# bucket, never the Pages bundle (see public/.assetsignore for the why).
*.glb
# EXCEPTION: the two Containment Lab characters. They are FIXTURES of the
# BSL-4 mini-game — every player is the researcher and becomes the sentinel —
# so they cannot live in a per-owner Storage bucket. 1.4 MB for the pair,
# already recompressed from 30 MB, and mirrored by an exception in
# public/.assetsignore so they actually reach the CDN.
!public/models/lab/researcher.glb
!public/models/lab/sentinel.glb
# EXCEPTION: the Cracking Yard's operator, for the same reason — every player
# who walks the yard IS this character, so it ships rather than living in a
# per-owner bucket. 0.75 MB, packed from three 8 MB Meshy exports by
# tools/glbpack-character.mjs. Mirrored in public/.assetsignore.
!public/models/refinery/guardian.glb
# EXCEPTION: the three trucks. Same rule again — these are CATALOGUE fixtures,
# not per-owner uploads: every player browsing Prince Portfolios' Truck Yard
# sees the same rigs, and the Cracking Yard's tanker is the model every
# refinery parks. A Storage bucket the player has never written to cannot
# serve a shop's own product photos. 1.2 MB for all three, packed from 364 MB
# and 9 million triangles of raw Meshy export by tools/glbprop.mjs.
# Mirrored in public/.assetsignore.
!public/models/trucks/tanker.glb
!public/models/trucks/freight_box.glb
!public/models/trucks/freight_rig.glb
# Oversized audio masters dropped into assets/Audio (~50-100 MiB each).
public/assets/Audio/*.wav
# Local-only working directories.
_legacy_vfx_backup/
public/.claude/
# Sibling projects that happen to sit inside this checkout — they are their
# own codebases and do not belong in the game's history.
mythic-contracts/
mythic-game-api/
.cityloop/
.battleloop/
.spriteloop/

# Oversized ANIMATED frames. .gif was not covered above, and this one is 112 MiB
# — past GitHub's 100 MiB hard per-file limit, so `git add` on it produces a
# rejected push rather than a large repo. It is already excluded from the
# Cloudflare upload for the same reason (public/.assetsignore). File stays on
# disk; compress or convert to a sprite sheet if it is ever wanted in-game.
public/assets/Units/unit frames/New units/*.gif

# Gauntlet debug captures. The screenshot harness lives in the session scratchpad
# and writes there; some builder agents nonetheless emit their isolated-bake PNGs
# and .meta.json probes to a shots/ dir at the repo root. That is 40MB+ of
# regenerable debug output per run and must never reach git history — the
# checkpoint commits during a wave use `git add -A`, so without this rule one
# stray bake lands in the repo permanently.
/shots/

# 🗄 Uncompressed asset masters (audio WAV, GLB, GIF) kept locally for
# re-encoding. 1.4 GB — never commit, never deploy. The shipped, compressed
# versions live under public/assets/. See migration/audit-report.md.
assets-source/

# Local run logs from the asset tooling.
migration/*.log
migration/*.err
# Gauntlet harness: vendored three.js + regenerable screenshots
.gauntlet/package/
.gauntlet/*.tgz
.gauntlet/shots/**/*.png
.gauntlet/progress.html

# Transient git worktrees created by in-flight Workflow builders — each is a
# full checkout and is removed when the run ends. Never commit these.
.claude/worktrees/
.gauntlet/patch-preview.html
# 15 MB pre-change snapshot rebuilt on demand by .gauntlet/_fxfind-baseline.mjs
.gauntlet/_fxfind-baseline.html
.gauntlet/probe-*.mjs
.gauntlet/shots/wip-*/
.gauntlet/shots/*.json

# Warehouse minigame headless capture output — regenerable.
_wh_shots/
scratchpad/

# ── Scratch and patch leftovers ────────────────────────────────────────────
# tmp/ is this repo's scratchpad: 678 files and ~300 MB of one-off screenshots
# and whole-file backups of index.html. None of it is source and none of it
# should ever have been a commit candidate.
tmp/

# 🔴 PATCH LEFTOVERS, AND THIS ONE WAS LIVE. `patch` writes a .orig beside the
# file it edits, and public/ is the deploy root — so a 15 MB copy of the entire
# game at v121q47 was being uploaded and served at /index.html.orig, where
# anyone could load a stale build. A second one had already shipped under
# node-city/. Ignored so the next stray patch cannot reach production.
*.orig
*.rej

# Athena Engine test harness — runtime folders created by setup.sh
tools/athena-harness/three/
tools/athena-harness/www/
tools/athena-harness/shots/
tools/athena-harness/artifact/
# EXCEPTION: the four hospital patients. Same rule as the lab characters and
# the trucks — these are FIXTURES every player sees, not per-owner uploads: the
# people who walk into your Medical Corporation are the same four looks for
# everybody, so a Storage bucket the player has never written to cannot serve
# them. ~3 MB for all four, packed from ~92 MB of raw Meshy export (four
# one-clip files each) by tools/glbpack-character.mjs.
# Mirrored in public/.assetsignore.
!public/models/hospital/patients/pilgrim.glb
!public/models/hospital/patients/survivor.glb
!public/models/hospital/patients/wanderer.glb
!public/models/hospital/patients/denim.glb

# 🏥 The hospital's fixtures as models (2026-09-04): two counters, four
# stations and the ward bed. 1.7–4.6 MB each, packed by tools/pack-glb.mjs
# from 115–128 MB Meshy exports whose masters stay in assets-source/ (ignored
# above). Each ships with a .json sidecar of measured extents that
# /public/src/hospital/floor.js and beds.js pin themselves to. Mirrored in
# public/.assetsignore.
!public/models/hospital/intake-desk.glb
!public/models/hospital/ward-desk.glb
!public/models/hospital/ward-bed.glb
!public/models/hospital/crate-intake.glb
!public/models/hospital/containment-vault.glb
!public/models/hospital/supply-bench.glb
!public/models/hospital/dispensary-stockroom.glb
!public/models/hospital/compounding-lab.glb
!public/models/hospital/loading-dock.glb
